Z||000000||TONY_C||05-16-2001||03:03 PM||||Does anyone know if the 12.5 gallon tanks from 85-88 fieros fit the 84 model?<BR>Thanks..||||reg||1
Z||000001||Galen||05-16-2001||06:09 PM||||Sadly it wont.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe Auto 4Banger - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR>AIM: WookieeNC||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||05-16-2001||06:21 PM||||The 84 thru 86 had 10.2 gallon gas tanks and the 87 and 88's had an 11.3 gallon tank. There is no 12.5 gallon tank in a Fiero and you can swap them but you need to swap out a bunch of stuff other than the tank. The mounts are the same but the hoses and lines are different.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 05-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Will||05-16-2001||07:52 PM||||I put the tank from an '87 into my '86. I had to "massage" the lip where the two pieces of the tank were welded together at the factory, and make my own clamp straps, but other than that everything was plug and play. I think I used the '86 fuel pump holder/associated hardware, and I definitely used a '96 Corvette pump.||||reg||1
